---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const calendly = 'https://calendly.com/contact-advised-seo/30min?back=1';
const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "WebPage",
      "url": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/recover-revenue-from-resellers/",
      "name": "Recover the revenue your resellers capture | AfriRank",
      "description": "Your brand is known, but it's your resellers cashing in on Google. AfriRank quantifies the leak and maps the plan to take back your direct sales.",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "isPartOf": { "@id": "https://www.afrirank.fr/#website" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "SEO for African & Black-owned brands", "item": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/seo-african-heritage-brands/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Recover the revenue your resellers capture", "item": "https://www.afrirank.fr/en/recover-revenue-from-resellers/" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "inLanguage": "en",
      "mainEntity": [
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "My brand is already well known — do I really need SEO?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Precisely because it's well known. Awareness creates the demand; SEO decides who cashes it in. A well-known brand whose resellers dominate Google is funding their growth with its own reputation." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Why do my resellers rank ahead of me?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Often an older domain, more indexed content, better-structured product pages and denser internal linking. Nothing unbeatable: these are gaps you can close." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "Is SEO for African & Black-owned brands different from regular SEO?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "The mechanics are the same, the terrain isn't: specific queries, competition from community marketplaces, and a real stake in showing up in AI answers. AfriRank is built for that terrain." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "How long before I see results?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Taking back your branded SERP is faster than conquering category queries. The Diagnostic prioritises the quickest wins first." } },
        { "@type": "Question", "name": "What happens after the Diagnostic?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "You have the numbers and the plan. Either you run it in-house, or you move into a Services engagement (the €290 is then credited)." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
});
---
<Base
  title="Recover the revenue your resellers capture | AfriRank"
  description="Your brand is known, but it's your resellers cashing in on Google. AfriRank quantifies the leak and maps the plan to take back your direct sales."
  lang="en"
  frPath="/recuperer-ca-revendeurs-google/"
  enPath="/en/recover-revenue-from-resellers/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}>

<section class="hero hero--page wrap">
  <div class="hero-top">
    <nav class="breadcrumb reveal" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/en/">Home</a><span class="sep">›</span>
      <a href="/en/seo-african-heritage-brands/">SEO for Black-owned brands</a><span class="sep">›</span>
      <span>Recover the revenue your resellers capture</span>
    </nav>
    <span class="hero-eyebrow reveal"><img src="/images/icon-orange.png" alt="" /> The leak</span>
    <h1 class="reveal">Your customers are searching for you. <em>It's your resellers cashing in.</em></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub reveal">Type your brand name into Google. Then your hero product. Watch who shows up above you: a reseller, a marketplace, a comparison site. The customer came for you. They buy from them.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:clamp(24px,4vw,48px)">
  <div class="wrap article reveal">
    <p class="lead">You pay twice. Once in the margin you give up to the wholesaler. A second time in losing the customer data, the repeat purchase, and control of your image. For an established African or Black-owned brand, this isn't an awareness problem. It's a <strong>capture</strong> problem.</p>

    <h2>The scenario every established heritage brand lives</h2>
    <p>You built the demand: years of word of mouth, community, presence in-store and on social. People know your name and search for your products.</p>
    <p>Except on Google, the page that answers that search isn't yours. It's a site with an older domain, more content, a better-optimised product page. It doesn't have your brand — it just took the spot that belonged to your brand.</p>
    <p>What that looks like in practice:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Someone searches "[your category]" → they land on a reseller, not you.</li>
      <li>They search "[your brand] [product]" → the marketplace sits above your own page.</li>
      <li>They ask ChatGPT or Perplexity → your brand isn't even mentioned.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Each of those searches is a sale you earned and someone else banks. <a href="/en/why-resellers-outrank-your-brand/">Why do your resellers rank ahead of you?</a></p>

    <h2>What it actually costs you</h2>
    <p>The leak is invisible because it shows up on no invoice. It hides in the gap between the demand your brand generates and the direct revenue you actually take in. Three losses stacked on top of each other:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>The margin.</strong> Every sale that goes to a reseller is your wholesale margin instead of your retail margin.</li>
      <li><strong>The customer.</strong> An indirect sale means no email, no repeat purchase, no loyalty programme. You're renting your own customer base.</li>
      <li><strong>The brand.</strong> When a third party owns your SERP, they dictate the price, the presentation and the experience attached to your name.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The exact figure depends on your volumes, your margins and how hard the capture bites on your queries. That's exactly what the Diagnostic quantifies — and you can already get a ballpark with the <a href="/en/lost-organic-revenue-calculator/">lost organic revenue calculator</a>.</p>

    <h2>What "taking back control" really means</h2>
    <p>Taking back control isn't "doing SEO". It's reclaiming three territories, in this order:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong><a href="/en/own-your-branded-serp/">Your branded SERP.</a></strong> When someone types your name, they should land on you — site, product pages, content — before any reseller.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="/en/reclaim-demand-from-marketplaces/">Your category queries.</a></strong> Non-branded searches should lead to your pages, not only to the marketplaces'.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="/en/ai-visibility-geo-black-brands/">Your presence in AI answers.</a></strong> ChatGPT, Perplexity and Google AI are becoming a buying entry point. A brand that isn't cited disappears from the recommendation.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The <em>what</em> and the <em>how much</em>, I show you. The <em>how</em> — the page-by-page execution — is the work of the engagement.</p>

    <h2>Why AfriRank</h2>
    <p>I'm Francis, an SEO consultant for 11 years. AfriRank does one thing: help established African and Black-owned brands stop funding their resellers' growth and bring that revenue back home. No jargon, no 80-page report nobody reads. A number on what you're losing, a map of where you're losing it, and a plan to take it back.</p>

    <blockquote><p>You leave with the number, even if you run the plan yourself.</p></blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head reveal"><span class="kicker">Frequently asked</span><h2 class="sec-title">Your questions, my answers.</h2></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">My brand is already well known — do I really need SEO? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Precisely because it's well known. Awareness creates the demand; SEO decides who cashes it in. A well-known brand whose resellers dominate Google is funding their growth with its own reputation.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Why do my resellers rank ahead of me? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Often an older domain, more indexed content, better-structured product pages and denser internal linking. Nothing unbeatable: these are gaps you can close.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">Is SEO for African & Black-owned brands different from regular SEO? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>The mechanics are the same, the terrain isn't: specific queries, competition from community marketplaces, and a real stake in showing up in AI answers. AfriRank is built for that terrain.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">How long before I see results? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>Taking back your branded SERP is faster than conquering category queries. The Diagnostic prioritises the quickest wins first.</p></div></div>
      <div class="faq-item reveal"><button class="faq-q">What happens after the Diagnostic? <span class="pm"></span></button><div class="faq-a"><p>You have the numbers and the plan. Either you run it in-house, or you move into a Services engagement (the €290 is then credited).</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="links-more reveal">
      <h2>Go further</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/en/seo-african-heritage-brands/">SEO strategy for African & Black-owned brands</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/own-your-branded-serp/">Own your branded SERP</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/lost-organic-revenue-calculator/">Estimate your lost organic revenue</a></li>
        <li><a href="/en/brand-visibility-scorecard/">Test your visibility score</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta-band reveal">
      <img src="/images/icon-cream.png" class="icon-watermark" alt="" />
      <h2>Start with the Diagnostic.</h2>
      <p>I quantify the organic revenue your resellers and marketplaces capture in your place, pinpoint your blind spots, and map the plan to win it back. €290 (~$310), fully credited toward your first month if you continue into a Services engagement.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href={calendly} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn--orange">Book the Diagnostic
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14M13 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
        </a>
        <a href="/en/seo-diagnostic/" class="btn btn--cream">Learn more</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Base>
